  "name": "Question 28",
  "problem": "Simplify the expression $[\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta -\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta ]^{6}.$",
  "worked_solution": "For expressions involving subtraction, De Moivre's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )]}^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\phi )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=6$ and $\\phi =3\\theta .$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta -\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta ]^{6} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\cdot 3\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\cdot 3\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(18\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(18\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
